ping using \"}]]}],\"$L80\",[\"$\",\"$3\",\"eca987a505da43a3a6ba0ee7cebf9f08\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"0\",{\"children\":\" and \"}]]}],\"$L81\",[\"$\",\"$3\",\"8be4c9bea7154564ab75d5401fd4238b\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"0\",{\"children\":\" with the maximum number of causal variants in a locus L = 10.\"}]]}]]}]\n7a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7307937aead445a98f0806be3bef0bd1\",{\"data-cover-aware-text\":\"\",\"className\":\"paragraph decoration-primary/6 max-w-3xl w-full print:break-inside-avoid text-start self-start justify-start\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"97b3bc3a0b8a4d618709d108427e846a\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"The \\\"Credible Sets\\\"-table on a phenotype page in the \"}]]}],\"$L82\",[\"$\",\"$3\",\"HJwfUDjx4R4p\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"0\",{\"children\":\" shows the SuSiE-fine-mapped credible sets of that phenotype. The variant shown per credible set is the maximum PIP (posterior inclusion probability) variant of that credible set. In addition to the causal variants, variants that were in sufficient LD (Pearson r^2 \u003e 0.05), had a small enough p-value (pval \u003c 0.01), and were close enough to the lead variant (distance to lead variant \u003c 1.5 megabases) were clumped together with the credible set. Variants have been compared against GWAS Catalog and annotated. The LD grouping, annotation and GWAS Catalog comparison were done using the autoreporting pipeline.\"}]]}]]}]\n7b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4bf5560dd300415985bc86bbee27b800\",{\"data-cover-aware-text\":\"\",\"className\":\"paragraph decoration-primary/6 max-w-3xl w-full print:break-inside-avoid text-start self-start justify-start\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"eaf33491f7d244db9f85ddaeed0743fc\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$3\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"The columns of the table are explained below:\"}]]}]]}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"$L83\",\"35d4637bf37e4116b68da11be418fca9\",{\"records\":[{\"id\":\"98d4075c0645499d972946ca1a16d05c\",\"searchText\":\"Column name Explanation\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"649a07f73dce4b6c9b92afbdc0cea995\",\"searchText\":\"top PIP variant variant with largest PIP int he credible set. Click the arrow to the left of the variant to show the credible set variants.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"33b337a244f14c06af9feb1ef41c44cb\",\"searchText\":\"CS quality This column shows whether the credible set is well-formed. a 'true' value means that the credible set is likely trustworthy, and a 'false' value means that the credible set is likely not trustworthy.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"fccb4bcca1eb4d019fda4443eed2bf8e\",\"searchText\":\"chromosome The chromosome in which the credible set lies.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"348b151092234dbab4d31ac358f3a1bb\",\"searchText\":\"position The position of the lead variant\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"c294d327db834f42842ba7c31af8270b\",\"searchText\":\"p-value p-value of the top PIP variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"914e67387b4149fea49207b165089416\",\"searchText\":\"-log10(p) -log10(p-value)\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"56153295fa4e46faa8a6c66d0d6ca0bb\",\"searchText\":\"effect size (beta) effect size of the top PIP variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"28e7ef1966c04030b2b83afdb20a3283\",\"searchText\":\"Finnish Enrichment Finnish enrichment of the top PIP variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"cf6a0fcda378454c97d2d01491ef5fc1\",\"searchText\":\"Alternate allele frequency alternate allele frequency of the top PIP variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"39fbebff4a444e7299c4aba85c2d1e71\",\"searchText\":\"Lead Variant Gene A probable gene of the top PIP variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"d653b45cef4e4719814b82749c809962\",\"searchText\":\"# coding in cs number of coding variants in the credible set. Hover over the number to see the variant, the consequence, and the correlation (pearsonr squared) to the lead variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"e73d3595649e465d8aa219c6333abaa8\",\"searchText\":\"# credible variants number of variants in the credible set.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"2f043c2a16834748a28d113997e09324\",\"searchText\":\"Credible set bayes factor (log10) The bayes factor related to the credible set.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"b93e4f2b6d004b61b7f59b4a08ee7938\",\"searchText\":\"CS matching Traits Number of matches found in GWAS Catalog for the credible set variants. Hover over the number to see the trait, as well as the associated variant's LD (pearsonr squared) to the lead variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}},{\"id\":\"46cd71b2dc5e4e668e82ffae2c63e105\",\"searchText\":\"LD Partner Traits Number of matches found in GWAS Catalog to the group of credible variants and variants in LD with the top PIP variant.Hover over the numbr to see the trait, as well as the associated variant's LD (pearsonr squared) to the lead variant.\",\"selectValues\":{},\"checkboxValues\":{}}],\"selectColumns\":[],\"recordGroups\":[[\"98d4075c0645499d972946ca1a16d05c\"],[\"649a07f73dce4b6c9b92afbdc0cea995\"],[\"33b337a244f14c06af9feb1ef41c44cb\"],[\"fccb4bcca1eb4d019fda4443eed2bf8e\"],[\"348b151092234dbab4d31ac358f3a1bb\"],[\"c294d327db834f42842ba7c31af8270b\"],[\"914e67387b4149fea49207b165089416\"],[\"56153295fa4e46faa8a6c66d0d6ca0bb\"],[\"28e7ef1966c04030b2b83afdb20a3283\"],[\"cf6a0fcda378454c97d2d01491ef5fc1\"],[\"39fbebff4a444e7299c4aba85c2d1e71\"],[\"d653b45cef4e4719814b82749c809962\"],[\"e73d3595649e465d8aa219c6333abaa8\"],[\"2f043c2a16834748a28d113997e09324\"],[\"b93e4f2b6d004b61b7f59b4a08ee7938\"],[\"46cd71b2dc5e4e668e82ffae2c63e105\"]],\"children\":\"$L84\"}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl layout-wide:max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full mt-6 flex flex-row flex-wrap